graphify-out/converted/behavior-spec_ed8c3838.md:29:| Progress API | PROGRESS-APP | As an authenticated player, I can fetch/save per-app progress and sync leaderboard scores. | GET validates appId and returns saved data or null; POST validates appId and Zod schema, optionally merges, upserts progress, extracts leaderboard score, creates profile/entry transactionally, and only updates better leaderboard scores. | Verified | Merge comments say server wins, but POST passes Date.now() as local timestamp, so merge can prefer local data over existing server data. | Fixed in iteration 1: merge=true no longer lets Date.now() local timestamp override existing server progress. | Sync semantics bug | apps/web/src/app/api/progress/[appId]/route.ts; apps/web/src/lib/progress-merge.ts; apps/web/src/lib/progress-schemas.ts; apps/web/src/lib/leaderboard-extractors.ts | Fix source: apps/web/src/app/api/progress/[appId]/route.ts; apps/web/src/shared/hooks/useAuthSync.ts; apps/web/src/lib/__tests__/progress-merge.test.ts | Route test existing server data plus merge:true; assert chosen data/conflicts | What conflict policy is intended: server-wins, local-wins, or field merge? | 1 | Iteration 1 static test/fix/re-test: merge POST no longer accepts/sends client localTimestamp and passes null local timestamp to mergeProgress when server data exists; focused progress merge tests passed 2 tests; full Vitest passed 8 files / 67 tests; tsc --noEmit and eslint --quiet passed. | 2026-06-27 |
